<title>GERMANY: BMW says not planning to buy Rolls-Royce.</title>
<headline>BMW says not planning to buy Rolls-Royce.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayerische Motoren-Werke AG (BMW) denied on Thursday that it held talks with Vickers Plc about buying the British company's Rolls-Royce car unit.</p>
<p>A BMW spokesman said speculation about such talks was &quot;absurd&quot;.</p>
<p>The Daily Mail newspaper has reported that Rolls-Royce chief executive Chris Woodwark met BMW director Walter Hasselkus in Britain on Monday to discuss a sale.</p>
<p>Vickers has also denied the report, calling it &quot;speculation and rumour&quot;.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
